# The port's half of the stage-1 proton like-for-like. Its partners are stage1_proton.mac and
# stage1_proton_noelastic.mac, run with ref/run/runb1.bat against the real Geant4 build of B1.
#
# NO /process/inactivate LINES, and that is the convention P1 set rather than an omission: this
# port's G4UImanager rejects an unknown command instead of ignoring it, so a macro that named
# Geant4's processes would fail here - and the two sides therefore cannot be the same file. What
# each side switches off is in its own file, next to the number it produced.
#
# NO STAGE COMMAND EITHER. The engine's HadronicStage defaults to kStage1, which is what these
# runs compare against, and there is no UI command for the other value on purpose: the final
# configuration refuses the at-rest capture of every stopped negative hadron by name (P12), so
# its dose is missing a rest mass per stopped track and is not a number to quote. When P12
# lands, TransportEngine::SetHadronicStage is the one line that changes.
#
# See stage1_README.md for what stage 1 is and why there are two Geant4-side macros.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 1

/gun/particle proton
/gun/energy 210 MeV

/run/beamOn 500000
